  "title": "tribus Pomptina",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/tribus"
  ],
  "details": "<p>The <em>tribus Pomptina</em> was placed <em>in agro Pomptino</em>, a region of Latium located between <em>Mons Albanus </em>and the Tyrrhenian coast. Control of the territory had passed to the Volsci in the late sixth century B.C., prompting Rome to reportedly begin establishing colonies - beginning with Norba - in the early fifth century B.C. Having reclaimed the <em>Ager Pomptinus </em>by 389 B.C., Rome established the colony of Setia ca. 382 B.C.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The tribus Pomptina (or Pontina) was a later rural tribe of Rome, which was established in 358 B.C.",
